meta {
  name: 11 Connection reuse and multiplexing
  seq: 12
}

docs {
  # Connection reuse & multiplexing
  
  The h2 session pool keeps **one session per (origin + TLS identity + proxy + mode)** and multiplexes every request onto it. Each response carries `x-connection-id` (server-side session/socket id) and `x-stream-id`.
  
  On h2:
  - Same origin → same connection id, and the stream id increases by 2 (client streams are odd).
  - Different origin (another hostname, even on the same IP:port) → a different session.
  - Parallel requests → one session, many streams.
  - After 30 s with no active streams, the session closes and the next request opens a new one (see **90 Slow**).
  
  On HTTP/1.1 the keep-alive agent also reuses sockets, but parallel requests open several sockets. The tests only assert the h2 behaviour.
}
